RAG query started for contextPrompt: 

 
Based on the following relevant information about candidates and their policies:

Top Issues: I am running for the Waitakere Ward to ensure your concerns are not only heard but acted upon. My priorities are clear:

•       Cap council rates to keep living affordable for all Aucklanders
•       Eliminate wasteful spending on non-core council business
•       Prioritise essential services: roads, rubbish, water, parks, and transport, and protect our Waitakere ranges.

Statement: A fresh face for Waitākere, but no stranger to council. I’ve been asked by friends and colleagues to bring my wealth of governance experience and excellent track record to our ward. 
I’ve worked in both private and public sectors across education, housing, and conservation. On council, I've led portfolios across transport, environment, and community development, where I’ve championed integration of climate action into decision making. From how we plan our neighbourhoods to how we strengthen local resilience. 
If elected, I’ll make sure your rates deliver you value.  I’ll defend the Ranges Heritage Area (Te Wao Nui-a-Tiriwa), support the Dark Sky initiative and making our beaches swim-safe. I’ll advocate for better upkeep of our roads and cheaper transport options for everyone. 
With your support, I’ll be your voice for a Waitākere that’s safer, more equitable, and genuinely great for all who live here. Vote for me and the Future West team.

Key Positions: Transport: Our public transport and roads must serve communities better.

1. Public transport must be reliable and accessible. I will advocate for lower fares, timely buses, and quicker development of transport hubs and stops.

2. Roads must be safe and efficient. I support fast responses to issues like potholes or a need for lights. I am for long-term planning, especially in growing neighbourhoods.

3. More and safer walkways and cycleways should be actioned. We should be able to get around without a car., Water: Our water systems should be adequate for our neighbourhoods.

1. Strengthening resilience to flooding. Upgrading infrastructure to ensure we are well protected in case of extreme weather.

2. Build wastewater, stormwater, and drinking water infrastructure that stands for generations.

Top Issues: Cost-of-living, housing, health dominate polls–Govt issues but your Local Board can deliver real wins. Priorities:
    1. Wellbeing: free pools, longer library hours, arts & culture connecting young & old, thriving local economy
    2. Water & Resilience: flood protection so homes & families are safe
    3. Environment & Transport: cut waste & pollution, more trees, influence smarter planning, the right public transport

Safe homes, strong communities & a cleaner, connected future matter for all

Key Positions: Transport: I want to ensure that advocacy for all modes is catered for, with focus on ensuring that people can park close to where they need to be, there is sufficient mobility parking available & our public transport is reliable and works in conjunction with other modes, Water: Water Care is the best organisation to deliver our water solutions, Healthy Waters is best placed to manage our storm water requirements. As local board it is our role to ensure they have the best information from us to ensure the work to the best of their abilities., Built environment: I am passionate about stopping urban sprawl and retaining our unique rural feel. The urban/rural boundary is a key focus of mine to ensure we build up and not out - where appropriate.

Key Positions: Transport: I will prioritise safer, well-maintained roads, better traffic flow, and improved public transport options that are reliable and affordable. I support expanding safe walking and cycling paths to connect neighbourhoods, reduce congestion, and promote healthier travel choices for all residents., Water: I support securing a sustainable water supply, maintaining high drinking water quality, and upgrading stormwater and wastewater systems to prevent flooding and pollution. Careful planning and investment are essential to safeguard our environment for future generations. Increasing in housing development in the area is pressurizing a need to ensure sufficient planning is done with the Services to ensure the current infrastructure able to sustain growth., Built environment: I support balanced urban development that delivers quality, affordable housing while protecting our heritage and green spaces. Investment in infrastructure must keep pace with growth, ensuring

Key Positions: Transport: Waitematā can have safe, affordable, and reliable transport. I’ll advocate for better public transport, safe cycling routes, and walkable streets, reduce traffic in residential areas, enforce safe speeds around schools, and make it easier for students, workers, and families to move around the city every day., Water: I’ll advocate for safe, sustainable water supply and effective wastewater management. We must protect our beaches and the Hauraki Gulf, invest in stormwater systems to prevent flooding, and ensure Waitematā’s water infrastructure is resilient and reliable., Built environment: I support more homes near where people work, study, and play, with well-planned, livable development that meets community needs. I back Council’s Housing First approach to reduce homelessness, and I will enhance and protect heritage, especially Māori heritage, while keeping our communities liveable, connected, and vibrant., Natural environment: I’ll work to expand green

Key Positions: Transport: My priorities are reliable, frequent public transport that serves working people; safe, connected cycleways that link neighborhoods and key destinations; and well-maintained walking tracks that support active lifestyles. I’ll push for smarter routes, better infrastructure, and planning that reflects how people actually move through our community., Water: My priorities for water infrastructure include upgrading aging systems to handle growth and climate impacts, improving stormwater management to reduce flooding, and expanding green solutions like rain gardens and wetlands. I support better coordination between council and communities, and promoting conservation through education and smart tools., Built environment: My priorities are balanced urban development that meets growth without losing character, affordable housing through smart planning and stronger protections, resilient infrastructure that supports future needs, and heritage protection that respects

Key Positions: Transport: “In Waitākere, we will work with Auckland Transport, iwi, Pasifika, and local communities to fix roads, improve buses and trains, and make public transport safer. We’ll create better walking and cycling links to schools, shops, and parks, with safe crossings, footpaths, and cycle lanes. These changes will cut congestion, protect our environment, and make travel safe, easy, and fair for everyone.” I am not for politics but for people, serving communities., Water: I will ensure Auckland’s water is safe, clean, and resilient. I’ll modernize wastewater and stormwater systems sustainably, protect our waterways and environment, and promote climate-resilient infrastructure. I will engage communities with education on water conservation and pollution prevention, working with local groups and iwi to ensure inclusive, responsible planning while building a modern, environmentally safe water system for all Aucklanders., Built environment: Auckland’s urban development

Why: Like all candidates I adore my home city. My family and I have lived in Westmere for 30 years, but I have stood back politically. Now, I want to work to make it the most future-capable, arts-positive, climate-resilient, infrastructurally able place to reside, travel, work and play. I want to ensure the Waitematā is clean, protected and valued, our waterways unpolluted and beaches swimmable. I will advocate for motorcycling and two wheeled transport as well as a fully integrated PT system.

